   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The composite has outer function F with \\( \\frac{d}{du} \\sqrt{u} = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} \\) and inner function \\( u = 13 - 3 x^{2} \\), whose derivative is \\( - 6 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "identify the layers"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = - \\frac{3 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{13 - 3 x^{2}}} + 2 x \\sqrt{13 - 3 x^{2}} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "product rule with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = -2 the inner value is 1 and the inner derivative is 12, so \\( h'(-2) = -4 + 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 12 = 20 \\).",
         "mathjson": 20,
